# Covers: tag.stop() on a strand parked in `waituntil` cancels the rest of
#         the tagged scope and resumes it after that scope.  The waiting
#         half of the body ("W") never runs; the statement after the scope
#         ("A") does.
# matrix-row: tag-stop
#
# HISTORY.  This fixture pinned "WA" under the old core's finish-then-drop
# rule: a stop deposit that landed after the target's last safepoint was
# DROPPED and the body completed.  The re-founded model has no deposit
# timing to lose a race with -- stop marks the strand, wakes it, and the
# strand unwinds itself at its next safepoint, which for a parked one is
# the moment it is woken.  A cancelled wait is cancelled.
## timeout: 30
## host: run var t = Tag.new()
## host: run Realm.flag = 0
## host: run Realm.log = ""
## host: run t: { waituntil(Realm.flag == 1); Realm.log = Realm.log + "W" }; Realm.log = Realm.log + "A"
## host: run t.stop()
## host: run Realm.log
## host: step 1000
[00000000] <Tag>
[00000000] 0
[00000000] ""
[00000000] nil
[00000000] nil
[00000000] "A"
[00000000] step: QUIESCENT
